✅ 18. What is async/await, and how is it used?
Async/await is a way to handle asynchronous operations in JavaScript. An async function always returns a Promise, and await pauses execution until that Promise is 
resolved or rejected. It makes asynchronous code cleaner and more readable, avoiding long .then() chains.


