✅ 39. How do you iterate over an array?
There are several ways to loop through an array:

const arr = [1, 2, 3];

// 1. standard for loop
for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
  console.log(arr[i]);
}

// 2. for...of loop (Modern and clean)
for (let num of arr) {
  console.log(num);
}

// 3. forEach method (Built-in array method)
arr.forEach((item) => console.log(item));

// 4. for...in loop (not recommended for arrays, better for objects)
for (let index in arr) {
  console.log(arr[index]);
}


