✅ 41. How do you handle errors in JavaScript?
JavaScript provides two main ways to handle errors: try…catch and .then().catch(). try…catch is used for synchronous code and is simple to use. .then().catch() is used 
for Promises in asynchronous code and allows handling errors effectively in async operations.

Hinglish:-

JavaScript me errors handle karne ke do main tareeke hote hain: try…catch aur .then().catch(). try…catch synchronous code ke liye use hota hai aur simple hota hai, jabki .then().catch()
Promises ke saath asynchronous code me use hota hai aur async operations me errors handle karne ke liye effective hota hai.

Synchronous:-
try {
  let result = riskyOperation();
  console.log(result);
} catch (error) {
  console.error("Error:", error.message);
}
Asynchronous:-
fetch("https://api.example.com")
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => console.log(data))
  .catch(error => console.error("Error:", error.message));


